<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.3: Admin Selects Landing Page for Creates Campaign S=
etup (Step-3)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to select a landing page template for my phishing ca=
mpaign, apply filters to narrow down the choices, preview the selected temp=
late, and finalize the landing page selection, so that I can configure the =
appropriate landing page for the phishing campaign.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>This use case describes the process by which the Aspire Admin selects a =
landing page template for the phishing campaign. The Admin can filter landi=
ng page templates based on various criteria (e.g., category, difficulty lev=
el) and preview the selected template before confirming it. The Admin has t=
he option to select between different types of landing pages, including the=
 <strong>Landing Page</strong>, <strong>Error/404 Page Not Found</strong>, =
and <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong>.</p>
<p>The Admin selects the relevant landing page template, and once selected,=
 the Admin can move on to the next step in the campaign setup. Additionally=
, the Admin can preview the landing page to ensure it meets the campaign's =
objectives before proceeding.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Selects the landing page, applies filters, previ=
ews the template, and proceeds to the next step.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays available landing page templates based=
 on applied filters, shows the preview of the selected template, and allows=
 the Admin to confirm their choice.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Admin is logged into the platform and has access to the <strong>Create N=
ew Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin is in the <strong>Landing Page Selection</strong> step.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p>The system has available landing page templates to choose from.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin has the option to select <strong>Landing Page</strong>, <stron=
g>Error/404 Page Not Found</strong>, or <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong=
>.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The selected landing page is confirmed for the phishing campaign.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled to proceed to=
 the next step in the campaign creation.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Navigate to Landing Page Selection</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin navigates to the <strong>Landing Page Selection</strong> step =
in the campaign creation wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the <strong>Landing Page Type</strong> options, incl=
uding <strong>Landing Page</strong>, <strong>Error/404 Page Not Found</stro=
ng>, and <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 2: Select Landing Page Type</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the <strong>Landing Page</strong> option from the radi=
o button.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>For <strong>Landing Page</strong>, the Admin can view available template=
s for phishing campaigns. p tag; Use predefined training pages to educate e=
mployees immediately after they fall for phishing. Shows what they should h=
ave noticed and provides security recommendations.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Alternatively, the Admin can choose <strong>Error/404 Page Not Found</st=
rong>. p tag: Use for "blind" phishing campaigns where users shouldn't know=
 it's a test. Shows a 404 error page, making it harder to suspect it's a se=
curity check.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Alternatively, the Admin can choose <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong>=
 for different types of campaigns. p tag: Redirect users to your own custom=
 training page. You take full responsibility for the content and availabili=
ty of this page.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 3: Select Geo Location</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the <strong>Geo Location</strong> from drop down<stron=
g>. </strong>Default Template Type is set to <strong>USA </strong>(United S=
tates, Canada, Brazil, Bangladesh, Australia, United Kingdom, Singapore, Ge=
rmany, Italy, Poland, Netherlands, Belgium, Mexico, Egypt, Algeria, Sudan, =
Saudi Arabia, Morocco, Indonesia, India, China). Other Geo Location will be=
 display in the list only if the Admin has added them dynamically from the =
setting.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 4: Select Template Type</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the <strong>Template Type</strong> from drop down<stro=
ng>. </strong>Default Template Type is set to <strong>All Templates </stron=
g>(Credential Harvesting, Financial Fraud, Malware Distribution, Data Theft=
, Account Takeover, Ransomware, Spyware, Business Email Compromise, Phishin=
g for Information, CEO Fraud). Other Template Type will be display in the l=
ist only if the Admin has added them dynamically from the setting.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 5: Search Template</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Admin can search the available Phishing Landing Page templates. placehol=
der: Search templates...<br>
Admin can search by keywords (e.g., "Holidays Offer").<br>
Admin can sort templates by popularity (Most to Least).<br>
Admin can search for templates using keywords.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 6: Apply Landing Page Filters</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks on the <strong>Apply Landing Page Filters</strong> butt=
on to apply filters such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the relevant filters such as <strong>Category</strong>=
 selected dropdown (Fake Login Page, Fake Payment Portal, Account Verificat=
ion Page, Social Media Clone Page, Fake Survey or Prize Giveaway Page, Fake=
 Technical Support Page, Fake E-commerce Checkout Page, Fake Invoice or Bil=
ling Page, Fake File Download Page, Fake Shipping or Tracking Page, Fake Su=
bscription Cancellation Page, Fake Security Alert Page, Fake Job Applicatio=
n Page, Fake Donation Page, Fake Software Update Page).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the <strong>Language </strong>from drop down<strong>. =
</strong>Default language is set to <strong>English</strong> (e.g., English=
, Spanish, Arabic, Bengali, Portuguese, French, Russian, Indonesian, Hindi,=
 Mandarin Chinese). Other language will be display in the list only if E-ma=
il template available in that language.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the <strong>Difficulty Level</strong>: Filters templat=
es based on difficulty (Easy, Medium, Hard).</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>After applying the filters, the system displays the available landing pa=
ge templates that match the selected criteria.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 7: View Available Landing Page Templates</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin reviews the available landing page templates under <strong>Ava=
ilable Landing Page Templates</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Templates are displayed with the template name, preview, and associated =
description (e.g., LinkedIn, Google Login, etc.).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can click <strong>Preview</strong> to view a preview of the la=
nding page.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use Pagination to Navigate Between Pages</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>The Admin can view the first page of 9 <strong>Available Landing Page</s=
trong>. After that it will show as pagination</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays pagination controls at the bottom of the campaign li=
st with the following options:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Previous</strong>: Navigate to the previous page.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Next</strong>: Navigate to the next page.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The page number (e.g., "1", "2", "3", etc.) is highlighted to indicate t=
he current page.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks <strong>Next</strong> or <strong>Previous</strong> to n=
avigate between pages of <strong>Available Landing Page</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system updates the page content and displays the <strong>Available L=
anding Page </strong>from the selected page.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Step 8: Preview Landing Page</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin clicks the <strong>Preview</strong> button next to a template.=
</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays a preview of the selected landing page, such as the =
LinkedIn login page example shown in the screenshot.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can review the page to ensure it fits the campaign's needs.</p=
></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 9: Close Preview</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After reviewing the preview, the Admin can close the preview window by c=
licking the <strong>Close</strong> button.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 10: Select Landing Page</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After previewing and reviewing the landing page, the Admin clicks <stron=
g>Select</strong> to confirm the selection of the landing page template for=
 the campaign.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 11: Proceed to Next Step</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Once the landing page is selected, the Admin can proceed to the next ste=
p by clicking <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Landing Page Type</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must select one of the three land=
ing page types (<strong>Landing Page</strong>, <strong>Error/404 Page Not F=
ound</strong>, or <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a valid landing page type=
."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Available Landing Page Templates</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory after applying filter=
s.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: At least one template must be selected from=
 the list after applying filters.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please select a landing page template."=
</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Preview</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: Admin can preview any selected template.</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: Admin must click <strong>Preview</strong> t=
o review the selected template before selecting it.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please preview the selected template be=
fore proceeding."</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"fb=
c6e98c-d639-42b8-a095-9a04125bcfc4" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must choose a <strong>Landing Page Type</strong> before selecting =
a template.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can filter available landing page templates based on <strong>Categ=
ory</strong> and <strong>Difficulty Level</strong>.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must <strong>Preview</strong> the selected template before confirm=
ing the selection.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Preview</strong> button must show an accurate representation=
 of the selected landing page.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-5</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must select one of the landing page types (Landing Page, <strong>E=
rror/</strong>404 Page Not Found, or Custom Landing Page).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-6</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system must show only the relevant templates after applying filters =
(e.g., <strong>Category</strong>, <strong>Difficulty Level</strong>).</p></=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-7</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must be able to <strong>Close</strong> the preview and return to t=
he selection screen.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-8</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must confirm their landing page selection by clicking <strong>Sele=
ct</strong>.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"dd=
2b03e6-9496-40dd-8f32-8d1d892fdfbb" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select a <strong>Landing Page Type</strong> (Landing Page, <st=
rong>Error/</strong>404 Page Not Found, Custom Landing Page).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>One of the three options must be selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply <strong>Landing Page Filters</strong> (Category, Difficu=
lty Level) to narrow down available templates.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Filters must correctly narrow down the templates displayed.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview a landing page template by clicking the <strong>Previe=
w</strong> button.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Preview of the selected landing page is displayed correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can close the preview window by clicking <strong>Close</strong>.</=
p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview window closes and returns to the template list.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can confirm their selection by clicking <strong>Select</strong>.</=
p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The selected template is confirmed and saved for the campaign.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can proceed to the next step after confirming the landing page sel=
ection.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled after selecti=
on.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system displays only relevant templates after applying the selected =
filters (Category, Difficulty Level).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Only templates matching the filter criteria are shown.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select a <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong> if that option i=
s chosen.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can enter a custom URL for the landing page if required.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must select a <strong>Landing Page Type</strong> before the <stron=
g>Save &amp; Continue</strong> button is enabled.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The button is disabled until a valid template is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select multiple templates if they are eligible to do so based =
on filters.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Multiple templates can be selected if permitted.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system prevents the Admin from proceeding without selecting a landin=
g page template.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Save &amp; Continue</strong> is only enabled once a valid templa=
te is selected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-12</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can apply filters (Category, Difficulty Level) and clear them usin=
g the <strong>Clear</strong> button.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The filters are applied and cleared successfully.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-13</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can view template names, descriptions, and preview images.</p></td=
>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Template details are visible in the list.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-14</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
